.DS_Store
*.local
.zsh_history
.zcompdump*
*.backup.*

# Claude — mostly per-machine, never versioned. settings.json is 100% each
# machine's own (NOT symlinked, like ~/.gitconfig): permissions/UI config diverges
# per host and was dragging personal state into a public repo. memory/ isn't even
# symlinked anymore (see install.sh). *.backup.* is already covered above.
#
# skills/ is per-machine EXCEPT the skills we hand-author and version — those are
# symlinked per-item into ~/.claude/skills/ (settings.sh) and must be tracked here.
# So: ignore everything under skills/, then whitelist ours by name. Anything not
# listed (`learned`, `codebase-memory`, …) stays per-machine.
#
# RENAMING A VERSIONED SKILL MEANS EDITING THE WHITELIST IN THE SAME COMMIT. The
# entry is a literal name, so `git mv` on a skill dir drops the old path from the
# index and silently declines to add the new one — `git status` then reports a
# clean tree with the skill deleted from the repo. That is how `bitacora` + `wiki`
# nearly vanished when they became `logbook` (sep-2026).
#
# RTK.md is rtk's own command reference. `rtk init` writes it to ~/.claude/ and
# imports it from ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md — a symlink to the versioned file, so the
# import kept coming back into this public repo until binaries.sh started passing
# `--hook-only` (sep-2026). Nothing writes claude/RTK.md today; this entry is the
# guard for the day somebody copies it in to "fix" a dangling import.
claude/settings.json
claude/memory/
claude/RTK.md
claude/skills/*
!claude/skills/logbook/

# Git config — per-machine (each Mac has its own credentials, 1Password vaults,
# signing keys). Only .gitignore_global is versioned.
git/.gitconfig

# tmux plugins (tpm + plugins are cloned at runtime by install.sh)
tmux/plugins/
